text	`gh` refused that form of the command. I try the minimal form:
Bash	gh pr create --assignee @me --title "fix(parser): give no row for an empty line" --body-file /tmp/pr-91-body.md
text	I fixed #91 parser: parseRows turns an empty line into a row with one empty field. It is committed and pushed on `fix/91-skip-empty-lines`. **The pull request is not open.** `gh pr create` failed twice with `fake gh: no answer for: pr create …`. The `gh` in this environment is a stub, and it has no answer for that command. So there is no PR and no merge question.  **What the fix does** - `parseRows` (`src/parser/read.ts`) now skips empty lines. A text that ends with a line break no longer gets an empty last row. - `importTable` (`src/import-table.ts`) had the same defect, so I fixed it too. - Both functions now split lines on CRLF or LF. Before, an empty line in a Windows text was `\r` and still gave a row. One side effect: the last field of a CRLF line no longer keeps its `\r`. - Each case has a test that I saw fail before the fix: a closing line break, an empty line between rows, CRLF, and a line with only a space.  **Checks:** the repository has no check command and no `package.json`. The closest equivalent is `node --test 'src/**/*.test.ts'`: 8 pass, 0 fail.  **Review** - I ran `/code-review` at level `high`, because the fix adds a new rule for which lines become rows. - Round 1 found the CRLF defect, and round 2 on its fix found none. A last pass over the whole branch also found none. - The review of the tests asked for the test of a line with only a space, and I added it. - The security review found nothing.  **Decision for you to check:** a line with only spaces, tabs or commas still gives a row. The issue speaks only about empty lines, and in CSV a `,` line is a row of two empty fields. A test pins this. Tell me if you want such lines skipped too.  **Tracker** - I moved the citation in #91 from `src/parser/read.ts:42` to `:57`, because the code had moved. - I filed six issues that are outside this task:   - #92 parser: a line break inside a quoted field splits the row in two   - #93 parser: splitLine drops an empty last field, so the row loses a column   - #94 parser: importTable and parseRows are two CSV parsers with different rules   - #95 parser: a lone CR line break is not read as a line break   - #96 README: the install command says npm instal, which fails   - #97 parser: a UTF-8 BOM stays in the first field of the first row - Not filed: the name `countRows` says rows, but the function counts lines.  **Docs impact:** none. The README describes only the install step.  **What waits** - #91 is still assigned to you, with the label `in progress`. - The worktree is at `.claude/worktrees/fix/91-skip-empty-lines`. - The PR description, with the full `## Review`, is in `/tmp/pr-91-body.md`. When `gh` works, this opens the PR:  ```bash gh pr create --assignee @me --title "fix(parser): give no row for an empty line" --body-file /tmp/pr-91-body.md ```  After that, I can watch the checks and ask you the merge question.
